1
00:00:00,957 --> 00:00:04,137
part 2 chapter 6.

2
00:00:04,137 --> 00:00:08,400
It had happened at last. The expected message had come.

3
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:12,540
All his life, it seemed to him, he had been waiting for this to happen.

4
00:00:12,540 --> 00:00:16,020
He was walking down the long corridor of the Ministry, and he was almost at the

5
00:00:16,020 --> 00:00:19,740
spot where Julia had slipped the note into his hand when he became aware that

6
00:00:19,740 --> 00:00:23,180
someone larger than himself was walking just behind him.

7
00:00:23,180 --> 00:00:28,619
The person, whoever it was, gave a small cough, evidently as a prelude to speaking.

8
00:00:28,619 --> 00:00:31,319
Winston stopped abruptly and turned.

9
00:00:31,319 --> 00:00:35,580
It was O'Brien At last they were face to face, and it

10
00:00:35,580 --> 00:00:38,040
seemed that his only impulse was to run away.

11
00:00:38,040 --> 00:00:42,840
His heart bounded violently. He would have been incapable of speaking.

12
00:00:42,840 --> 00:00:47,099
O'Brien, however, had continued forward in the same movement, laying a friendly hand

13
00:00:47,099 --> 00:00:51,718
for a moment on Winston's arm, so that the two of them were walking side by side.

14
00:00:51,718 --> 00:00:55,560
He began speaking with the peculiar grave courtesy that differentiated him

15
00:00:55,560 --> 00:00:58,319
from the majority of Inner Party members.

16
00:00:58,319 --> 00:01:02,939
'I had been hoping for an opportunity of talking to you,' he said. 'I was reading one

17
00:01:02,939 --> 00:01:06,180
of your Newspeak articles in the Times the other day.

18
00:01:06,180 --> 00:01:10,319
You take a scholarly interested Newspeak, I believe?'

19
00:01:10,319 --> 00:01:15,779
Winston had recovered part of his self-position Hardly scholarly,' he said. 'I'm only an

20
00:01:15,779 --> 00:01:19,979
amateur. It's not my subject. I have never had anything to do with the actual

21
00:01:19,979 --> 00:01:22,200
construction of the language.'

22
00:01:22,200 --> 00:01:26,400
'But you write it very elegantly,' said O'Brien. 'That is not only my own opinion.

23
00:01:26,400 --> 00:01:30,540
I was talking recently to a friend of yours who was certainly an expert. His

24
00:01:30,540 --> 00:01:32,939
name has slipped my memory for the moment.'

25
00:01:32,939 --> 00:01:35,637
Again Winston's heart stirred painfully.

26
00:01:35,637 --> 00:01:39,779
It was inconceivable that this was anything other than a reference to Sam

27
00:01:39,779 --> 00:01:43,439
But Simon was not only dead, he was abolished, an unperson.

28
00:01:43,439 --> 00:01:47,580
Any identifiable reference to him would have been mortally dangerous

29
00:01:47,580 --> 00:01:52,319
her Brand's remark must obviously have been intended as a signal, a code word

30
00:01:52,319 --> 00:01:55,740
By sharing a small act of thought crime he had to turn to the two of them into

31
00:01:55,740 --> 00:01:57,479
accomplices.

32
00:01:57,479 --> 00:02:02,819
They had continued to stroll slowly down the corridor, but now O'Brien halted. With

33
00:02:02,819 --> 00:02:06,180
the curious, disarming friendliness that he always managed to put into the

34
00:02:06,180 --> 00:02:11,159
gesture, he resettled his spectacles on his nose. Then he went on:

35
00:02:11,159 --> 00:02:15,180
'What I had really intended to say was that in your article I noticed you had

36
00:02:15,180 --> 00:02:17,580
used two words which have become obsolete.

37
00:02:17,580 --> 00:02:21,360
But they have only become so very recently. Have you seen the tenth edition

38
00:02:21,360 --> 00:02:23,878
of the Newspeak Dictionary?'

39
00:02:23,878 --> 00:02:27,599
'No,' said Winston. 'I didn't think it had been issued yet. We are still using the

40
00:02:27,599 --> 00:02:30,119
ninth in the Records Department.'

41
00:02:30,119 --> 00:02:33,957
'The 10th edition is not due to appear for some months, I believe. But a few

42
00:02:33,957 --> 00:02:37,797
Advanced copies have been circulated. I have one myself. It might interest you to

43
00:02:37,797 --> 00:02:39,479
look at it, perhaps?'

44
00:02:39,479 --> 00:02:43,860
'Very much so,' said Winston, immediately seeing where this tended.

45
00:02:43,860 --> 00:02:47,700
'Some of the new developments are most ingenious. The reduction in the number of

46
00:02:47,700 --> 00:02:49,619
verbs— —that is the point that will appeal

47
00:02:49,619 --> 00:02:54,060
to you, I think. Let me see, shall I send a messenger to you with the Dictionary?

48
00:02:54,060 --> 00:02:57,180
But I'm afraid I invariably forget anything of that kind.

49
00:02:57,180 --> 00:03:01,500
Perhaps you could pick it up at my flat at some time that's suited you? Wait. Let

50
00:03:01,500 --> 00:03:03,540
me give you my address.'

51
00:03:03,540 --> 00:03:08,457
They were standing in front of a Telly screen Somewhat absent-mindedly a brand felt

52
00:03:08,457 --> 00:03:13,619
two of his pockets and then produced a small leather covered notebook and a gold ink pencil

53
00:03:13,619 --> 00:03:17,040
Immediately beneath the telescreen, in such a position that anyone who was

54
00:03:17,040 --> 00:03:19,378
watching at the other end of the instrument could read what he was

55
00:03:19,378 --> 00:03:24,779
writing, he scribbled an address, tore out the page and handed it to Winston

56
00:03:24,779 --> 00:03:28,740
I'm usually at home in the evenings,' he said. 'If not, my servant will give you the

57
00:03:28,740 --> 00:03:31,020
Dictionary.'

58
00:03:31,020 --> 00:03:34,619
He was gone, leaving Winston holding the scrap of paper, which this time there was

59
00:03:34,619 --> 00:03:38,637
no need to conceal. Nevertheless he carefully memorized what was written on

60
00:03:38,637 --> 00:03:44,340
it, and some hours later dropped it into the memory hole along with a mass of other papers.

61
00:03:44,340 --> 00:03:47,819
They had been talking to one another for a couple of minutes at the most.

62
00:03:47,819 --> 00:03:51,659
There was only one meaning that the episode could possibly have. It had been

63
00:03:51,659 --> 00:03:55,200
contrived as a way of letting Winston know a Brand's address.

64
00:03:55,200 --> 00:03:59,279
This was necessary, because except by direct inquiry it was never possible to

65
00:03:59,279 --> 00:04:01,500
discover where anyone lived.

66
00:04:01,500 --> 00:04:03,957
There were no directories of any kind.

67
00:04:03,957 --> 00:04:05,700
'If you ever want to see me this is where

68
00:04:05,700 --> 00:04:09,060
I can be found,' was what O'Brien had been saying to him.

69
00:04:09,060 --> 00:04:12,119
Perhaps there would even be a message concealed somewhere in the Dictionary.

70
00:04:12,119 --> 00:04:14,878
But at any rate, one thing was certain.

71
00:04:14,878 --> 00:04:19,919
The conspiracy that he had dreamed of did exist, and he had reached the outer edges of it.

72
00:04:19,919 --> 00:04:23,637
He knew that sooner or later he would obey O'Brien's summons.

73
00:04:23,637 --> 00:04:27,900
Perhaps tomorrow, perhaps after a long delay— —he was not certain.

74
00:04:27,900 --> 00:04:32,340
What was happening was only the working out of a process that had started years ago.

75
00:04:32,340 --> 00:04:35,939
The first step had been a secret, involuntary thought, the second had been

76
00:04:35,939 --> 00:04:37,680
the opening of the diary.

77
00:04:37,680 --> 00:04:42,779
He had moved from thoughts to words, and now from words to actions. The last step

78
00:04:42,779 --> 00:04:47,099
was something that would happen in the Ministry of Love. He had accepted it.

79
00:04:47,099 --> 00:04:49,439
The end was contained in the beginning.

80
00:04:49,439 --> 00:04:53,457
But it was frightening: or, more exactly, it was like a foretaste

81
00:04:53,457 --> 00:04:56,400
of death, like being a little less alive.

82
00:04:56,400 --> 00:04:59,457
Even while he was speaking to O'Brien with the meaning of the words that

83
00:04:59,457 --> 00:05:04,080
sunken a chilly shuddering feeling had taken possession of his body

84
00:05:04,080 --> 00:05:08,099
the sensation of stepping into the dampness of a grave, and it was not much

85
00:05:08,099 --> 00:05:12,000
better because he had always known that the grave was there and waiting for him
